    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-internationally-protected-persons-act-1976-article-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 1. The intentional commission of:",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-internationally-protected-persons-act-1976#article-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-internationally-protected-persons-act-1976.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-internationally-protected-persons-act-1976.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "(a) a murder, kidnapping or other attack upon the person or liberty of an\ninternationally protected person;\n\n(b) a violent attack upon the official premises, the private accommodation\nor the means of transport of an internationally protected person likely to\nendanger his person or liberty;\n\n(c) a threat to commit any such attack;\n\n(d) an attempt to commit any such attack; and\n\n(e) an act constituting participation as an accomplice in any such attack\nshall be made by each State Party a crime under its internal law.\n2. Each State Party shall make these crimes punishable by appropriate\npenalties which take into account their grave nature.\n3. Paragraphs 1 and 2 of this article in no way derogate from the obligations\nof States Parties under international law to take all appropriate measures to\nprevent other attacks on the person, freedom or dignity of an internationally\nprotected person.",
      "skos:definition": "(a) a murder, kidnapping or other attack upon the person or liberty of an\ninternationally protected person;\n\n(b) a violent attack upon the official premises, the private accommodation\nor the means of transport of an internationally protected person likely to\nendanger his person or liberty;\n\n(c) a threat to commit any such attack;\n\n(d) an attempt to commit any such attack; and\n\n(e) an act constituting participation as an accomplice in any such attack\nshall be made by each State Party a crime under its internal law.\n2. Each State Party shall make these crimes punishable by appropriate\npenalties which take into account their grave nature.\n3. Paragraphs 1 and 2 of this article in no way derogate from the obligations\nof States Parties under international law to take all appropriate measures to\nprevent other attacks on the person, freedom or dignity of an internationally\nprotected person.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-internationally-protected-persons-act-1976-article-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-internationally-protected-persons-act-1976-article-2-logic-deontic-1"
