    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-internationally-protected-persons-act-1976-article-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 1. Each State Party shall take such measures as may be necessary to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-internationally-protected-persons-act-1976#article-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-internationally-protected-persons-act-1976.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-internationally-protected-persons-act-1976.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "establish its jurisdiction over the crimes set forth in article 2 in the following\ncases:\n\n(a) when the crime is committed in the territory of that State or on board a\nship or aircraft registered in that State;\n\n(b) when the alleged offender is a national of that State;\n\nConvention on the prevention and punishment of crimes against internationally\nprotected persons, including diplomatic agents  Schedule\n\nCrimes (Internationally Protected Persons) Act 1976\nCompilation date: 10/3/16\nRegistered: 26/5/16\n\n(c) when the crime is committed against an internationally protected person\nas defined in article 1 who enjoys his status as such by virtue of\nfunctions which he exercises on behalf of that State.\n2. Each State Party shall likewise take such measures as may be necessary\nto establish its jurisdiction over these crimes in cases where the alleged offender\nis present in its territory and it does not extradite him pursuant to article 8 to any\nof the States mentioned in paragraph 1 of this article.\n3. This Convention does not exclude any criminal jurisdiction exercised in\naccordance with internal law.",
      "skos:definition": "establish its jurisdiction over the crimes set forth in article 2 in the following\ncases:\n\n(a) when the crime is committed in the territory of that State or on board a\nship or aircraft registered in that State;\n\n(b) when the alleged offender is a national of that State;\n\nConvention on the prevention and punishment of crimes against internationally\nprotected persons, including diplomatic agents  Schedule\n\nCrimes (Internationally Protected Persons) Act 1976\nCompilation date: 10/3/16\nRegistered: 26/5/16\n\n(c) when the crime is committed against an internationally protected person\nas defined in article 1 who enjoys his status as such by virtue of\nfunctions which he exercises on behalf of that State.\n2. Each State Party shall likewise take such measures as may be necessary\nto establish its jurisdiction over these crimes in cases where the alleged offender\nis present in its territory and it does not extradite him pursuant to article 8 to any\nof the States mentioned in paragraph 1 of this article.\n3. This Convention does not exclude any criminal jurisdiction exercised in\naccordance with internal law.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-internationally-protected-persons-act-1976-article-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-internationally-protected-persons-act-1976-article-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5e4015d116d35754cafe1f10c48f242aa918c3a2bc64d36f9da7f52b6653a99a",
      "skos:note": "Each State Party shall take measures to establish jurisdiction over crimes against internationally protected persons."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-internationally-protected-persons-act-1976#article-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 1. Each State Party shall take such measures as may be necessary to",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "establish its jurisdiction over the crimes set forth in article 2 in the following\ncases:\n\n(a) when the crime is committed in the territory of that State or on board a\nship or aircraft registered in that State;\n\n(b) when the alleged offender is a national of that State;\n\nConvention on the prevention and punishment of crimes against internationally\nprotected persons, including diplomatic agents  Schedule\n\nCrimes (Internationally Protected Persons) Act 1976\nCompilation date: 10/3/16\nRegistered: 26/5/16\n\n(c) when the crime is committed against an internationally protected person\nas defined in article 1 who enjoys his status as such by virtue of\nfunctions which he exercises on behalf of that State.\n2. Each State Party shall likewise take such measures as may be necessary\nto establish its jurisdiction over these crimes in cases where the alleged offender\nis present in its territory and it does not extradite him pursuant to article 8 to any\nof the States mentioned in paragraph 1 of this article.\n3. This Convention does not exclude any criminal jurisdiction exercised in\naccordance with internal law."
    },
    {
