      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-internationally-protected-persons-act-1976.pdf, p.21",
      "values:originalText": "in connexion with criminal proceedings brought in respect of the crimes set\nforth in article 2, including the supply of all evidence at their disposal necessary\nfor the proceedings.\n2. The provisions of paragraph 1 of this article shall not affect obligations\nconcerning mutual judicial assistance embodied in any other treaty.\n\nSchedule  Convention on the prevention and punishment of crimes against\ninternationally protected persons, including diplomatic agents\n\nCrimes (Internationally Protected Persons) Act 1976\n\nCompilation date: 10/3/16\nRegistered: 26/5/16",
      "skos:definition": "in connexion with criminal proceedings brought in respect of the crimes set\nforth in article 2, including the supply of all evidence at their disposal necessary\nfor the proceedings.\n2. The provisions of paragraph 1 of this article shall not affect obligations\nconcerning mutual judicial assistance embodied in any other treaty.\n\nSchedule  Convention on the prevention and punishment of crimes against\ninternationally protected persons, including diplomatic agents\n\nCrimes (Internationally Protected Persons) Act 1976\n\nCompilation date: 10/3/16\nRegistered: 26/5/16",
